From 2d1992b6960beb18cf7110c451cfeb09123af588 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mat Kowalski <mko@redhat.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 12:16:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] machineconfiguration/v1: bound BGPVIPPeersJSON length and
 refresh openapi

Address review feedback:
- Add MinLength=1/MaxLength=65536 to BGPVIPPeersJSON to satisfy the
  kube-api-linter maxlength and minlength rules. 64Ki is sized for
  large multi-rack peer sets (cf. 32Ki used for MachineConfigNode
  error blobs).
- Refresh openapi/openapi.json via hack/update-openapi.sh; the update
  target does not run this script, so the file also carried drift from
  master (TLS groups/profile and kube-state-metrics doc updates) in
  addition to the vipManagement field from the parent commit.
---
 machineconfiguration/v1/types.go              |  3 ++
 ...controllerconfigs-CustomNoUpgrade.crd.yaml |  3 ++
 ...rollerconfigs-DevPreviewNoUpgrade.crd.yaml |  3 ++
 .../BGPBasedVIPManagement.yaml                |  3 ++
 .../v1/zz_generated.swagger_doc_generated.go  |  2 +-
 openapi/openapi.json                          | 46 ++++++++++++++-----
 ...controllerconfigs-CustomNoUpgrade.crd.yaml |  3 ++
 ...rollerconfigs-DevPreviewNoUpgrade.crd.yaml |  3 ++
 8 files changed, 53 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

